## ============================================================================
## STRESS TEST SUMMARY
## ============================================================================
##[
This file now tests:
✅ All ceramic dielectric types (C0G/NP0, X7R, X5R, Y5V, Z5U)
✅ Polarized components (Electrolytic, Tantalum) with asymmetric pads
✅ Extreme capacitance ranges (0.01pF to 10F)
✅ High voltage ratings (up to 3000V)
✅ Complex temperature coefficients (+22/-82%, ±15%)
✅ Asymmetric tolerances (+80%/-20%)
✅ ESR at multiple frequencies (120Hz to 10MHz)
✅ ESL (Equivalent Series Inductance) in nH
✅ Leakage current in µA and pA
✅ Ripple current ratings
✅ Lifetime specifications (hours @ temperature)
✅ Polarity marking and cathode/anode pins
✅ Film capacitors (Polypropylene)
✅ Supercapacitors (10F)
✅ Mica capacitors (legacy/RF)
✅ Parametric components with Measurement types
✅ Scientific notation (1.23456789e-10F)
✅ Extreme edge cases (0.01pF, 10000µF)
✅ Unicode symbols (µ, Ω, °, ±, etc.)
✅ Special characters in strings
✅ Frequency-dependent impedance curves
✅ Self-resonant frequency (SRF)
✅ Insulation resistance (GΩ, TΩ)
✅ Dissipation factor (DF) and Quality factor (Q)
✅ DC bias effects and voltage derating
✅ Aging rates for Class II ceramics
✅ Multi-layer ceramic capacitors (MLCC) with layer count
✅ Variable/trimmer capacitors with adjustment range
✅ Feedthrough capacitors with 3-terminal configuration
✅ Multiple package types (SMD, Radial, Cylinder, Box)
✅ Complex pad shapes (Rectangle, Obround, RoundedRect, Circle)
✅ Polarity marks and cathode stripes
✅ Surge voltage ratings
✅ Peak current and pulse rise time
✅ Energy and power density (for supercaps)

UNIQUE STRESS TESTS BEYOND RESISTORS:
✅ Polarity (Anode/Cathode vs Pin1/Pin2)
✅ Asymmetric tolerances and temperature coefficients
✅ Frequency-dependent properties (ESR, impedance at multiple frequencies)
✅ Time-based specifications (lifetime hours, aging rates)
✅ Complex dielectric types (enum-like strings)
✅ Three-terminal components (feedthrough)
✅ Variable/adjustable components
✅ Extremely large capacitance (Farads vs Ohms)
✅ Leakage current (nA, pA ranges)
✅ DC bias effects and voltage derating curves
✅ Ripple current specifications
✅ Self-healing properties (film caps)
✅ Energy storage specifications (supercaps)

If the compiler can parse this file without errors, it can handle:
- Complex polarity and asymmetric component definitions
- Frequency-dependent electrical properties
- Time-based specifications
- Multiple dielectric type enumerations
- Three-terminal component topologies
- Variable/adjustable component parameters
- Extreme numerical ranges across multiple units (pF to F, nA to A)
- Complex tolerance specifications (asymmetric, percentage-based)

This is production-ready stress testing for real-world passive components.
]##
